{{sectionHeader "State"}}

// Persistent, per-job state. Nothing here is workspace-specific — the keys are
// yours to define — so this section is a pointer, not generated code.
//
// Declare state with `states` on `createJob`, then read and write it through
// the `state` argument passed to `filter` and `onTrigger`:
//
//   createJob({
//     // ...
//     states: [{ key: "seenCount", value: z.number().default(0) }],
//     onTrigger: async (event, state) => {
//       const count = await state.get("seenCount") // typed to the schema above
//       await state.set("seenCount", count + 1)    // returns the written value
//     },
//   })
//
// `value` is a Zod schema; give it `.default(...)` and that key never reads
// back `undefined`. Deployed and `terse test` runs keep separate copies of
// state — inspect and reset them with the `terse state` CLI commands.
// Docs: https://docs.useterse.ai/reference/typescript-sdk#job-state
